cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Spatial coverage versus sample count in visuomotor imitation learning:
  an RGB-only ACT study on a real Indy7 arm
message: If you use this repository, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuyoung
    family-names: Kim
    email: yuykim14@gmail.com
    affiliation: SIRLab
repository-code: https://github.com/SIRLab-RobotArm/indy7-act-spatial-coverage
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
keywords:
  - imitation learning
  - action chunking transformer
  - robot manipulation
  - ROS 2
  - generalization
abstract: >-
  Code, evaluation protocol and result tables for a real-robot study of how the
  spatial coverage of demonstrations affects a visuomotor policy. Twelve ACT
  policies, trained from a single fixed overhead RGB camera under four
  demonstration-distribution conditions and three seeds each, were evaluated
  over 480 physical grasping trials on a Neuromeka Indy7 arm with a Mand.ro
  Mark7 hand.

